# Aromatic Salt Additive Molecules (Water‑Phase)

Sodium_Benzoate
  Formula: C6H5COO⁻ Na⁺
  Type: Aromatic carboxylate salt
  Notes: Highly water‑soluble; forms clear saline/aromatic solution.

Sodium_Salicylate
  Formula: C6H4(OH)COO⁻ Na⁺
  Type: Aromatic phenolic carboxylate salt
  Notes: Dissolves strongly in water + ethanol; non‑volatile.

Sodium_Toluene_Sulfonate
  Formula: CH3–C6H4–SO3⁻ Na⁺
  Type: Aromatic sulfonate salt
  Notes: Very polar; excellent water solubility; detergent‑like behavior.

Potassium_Benzoate
  Formula: C6H5COO⁻ K⁺
  Type: Aromatic carboxylate salt
  Notes: Similar to sodium benzoate; dissolves instantly in water.

Sodium_Phenolate
  Formula: C6H5O⁻ Na⁺
  Type: Aromatic phenoxide salt
  Notes: Strong base; dissolves in water/ethanol; not fuel‑phase.

Sodium_Anisate
  Formula: CH3O–C6H4–COO⁻ Na⁺
  Type: Aromatic methoxy carboxylate salt
  Notes: Water‑soluble aromatic salt; stays in aqueous phase.

Sodium_Cinnamate
  Formula: C6H5–CH=CH–COO⁻ Na⁺
  Type: Aromatic alkene carboxylate salt
  Notes: Dissolves in water/ethanol; non‑volatile.
